{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789420360,"nonce":"IC2EOu6R/xDhIeDLC2dpZpXPq9w=","title":"Compiled Url.parse runs past a Fiber.abort under GC stress","message":"cd hatch/packages/hatch-url\n    HATCH_OFFLINE=1 WLIFT_GC_STRESS=1 wlift --mode tiered \\\n        --jit-threshold 1 --opt-threshold 4 url.spec.wren\n\nfails the three \"parse: errors\" cases in about a third of runs at\n8a0f684 (before the scheduler and the M:N work) and in nearly every\nrun at a2f75e5: the abort raised inside the compiled `parse` is not\nhonoured and the function goes on to slice with a NaN bound\n(\"String slice 2..NaN out of bounds\", \"Subscript must be a number or\nrange\"). Plain GC stress, or the hot thresholds without stress, pass;\nthe interpreter passes. So it is the compiled error path when a\ncollection lands inside or right after the abort's native call —\nwhich of `has_error`/`last_error`/the pending fiber state the compiled\ncaller checks after a native returns, and what the collection resets.\nFound 2026-09-14 running the corpus after the M:N stage 3; the\ncorpus's hot+stress pass recorded earlier was the seventy percent.","files":null}]}